    "Applying ladder edits…": "dex.makerApplying",
    "Finishing the current adjustment; withdrawal will then be attempted. Check Orders for confirmation.": "dex.makerWithdrawQueued",
    "No ladder orders to withdraw": "dex.makerNothingWithdraw",
    "Withdrawing the ladder — cancels leave the book as blocks confirm them": "dex.makerWithdrawing",
    "Maker settings changed in another session. Reload and review them before saving again.": "dex.makerSettingsConflict",
    "Maker settings could not be saved. Check available storage.": "dex.makerSaveFailed",
    "PEGGED: prices track the MEXC mid and reprice when it moves past your threshold; your per-rung sizes are kept. If the feed goes stale the app widens its quotes, then requests withdrawal. Existing orders remain tradeable until cancellation confirms.": "dex.makerPeggedConsent",
    "NOT pegged: the book gets YOUR exact prices — never repriced, never withdrawn, even if the price feed dies.": "dex.makerManualConsent",
    "Rungs post ONE PER SIDE per cycle — each is an on-chain transaction your phone does proof-of-work for, and each one's change has to confirm before the next on that side can be funded — so a full ladder takes a few minutes to build and a rung may retry before it sticks. The Maker tab shows each rung's progress.": "dex.makerPostingConsent",
    "Background checks are normally requested every 15 minutes. Android may delay or stop them, so automatic withdrawal is not a guaranteed price limit. Keep PandaDEX and MinimaCore running while monitoring the ladder; check Orders for confirmed cancellations.": "dex.makerBackgroundConsent",
    "Rungs post one per side per cycle, so a large batch lands over a few minutes. The status panel shows each one.": "dex.makerEditTiming",
